# HR360 — Frontend Architecture Document

**Document ID:** HR360-FE-001
**Version:** 1.0
**Status:** Draft for Review
**Date:** 20 September 2026
**Project:** HR360 — Human Resource Management & Analytics System
**Prepared By:** Nida Khan
**Business Analyst / Developer / Project Manager / Scrum Master:** Nida Khan
**Product Owner:** HR Business Stakeholder

---

## 1. Document Purpose

This document defines the frontend architecture for the HR360 Human Resource Management & Analytics System.

The purpose is to establish a structured, scalable, maintainable and user-friendly React frontend that integrates with the existing Node.js/Express backend APIs and PostgreSQL database layer.

The frontend will provide HR, Operations, Finance, Recruitment and management users with access to employee management, workforce operations, attendance, leave, performance, training, recruitment and analytics functionality.

---

## 2. Frontend Objectives

The HR360 frontend shall:

1. Provide a professional HR management interface.
2. Consume backend REST APIs through controlled API services.
3. Provide role-oriented navigation and functionality.
4. Display employee and workforce information clearly.
5. Support CRUD operations where backend APIs are available.
6. Display department-specific employee active status.
7. Provide dashboards and analytical visualizations.
8. Provide consistent validation and error handling.
9. Support responsive desktop and tablet layouts.
10. Maintain clear separation between UI, business interaction logic and API communication.
11. Support future authentication and authorization.
12. Support future Power BI integration.

---

## 3. Technology Stack

| Layer              | Technology                               |
| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |
| Frontend Framework | React                                    |
| Build Tool         | Vite                                     |
| Language           | JavaScript                               |
| Styling            | CSS / responsive CSS                     |
| API Communication  | Fetch API or Axios                       |
| Routing            | React Router                             |
| Charts             | Chart library / visualization components |
| Backend            | Node.js + Express.js                     |
| Database           | PostgreSQL 18                            |
| API Style          | REST                                     |
| Version Control    | Git / GitHub                             |
| BI Integration     | Power BI                                 |
| Development IDE    | Visual Studio Code                       |

Python is not required for the frontend implementation.

---

## 4. Frontend Logical Architecture

The frontend follows a layered component architecture:

```text
User
  |
  v
React Application
  |
  +----------------------+
  | Presentation Layer   |
  | Pages / Components   |
  +----------------------+
             |
             v
  +----------------------+
  | Application Layer    |
  | State / UI Logic     |
  +----------------------+
             |
             v
  +----------------------+
  | API Service Layer    |
  | REST API Calls       |
  +----------------------+
             |
             v
  +----------------------+
  | HR360 Backend        |
  | Node.js / Express    |
  +----------------------+
             |
             v
  +----------------------+
  | PostgreSQL Database  |
  +----------------------+
```

---

