The frontend shall consume the HR360 analytics APIs.

Available analytics endpoints:

```text
/api/analytics/overview
/api/analytics/departments
/api/analytics/attendance
/api/analytics/leave
/api/analytics/performance
/api/analytics/training
/api/analytics/recruitment
```

The analytics interface shall support:

* KPI cards
* Department charts
* Attendance charts
* Leave charts
* Performance charts
* Training charts
* Recruitment charts
* Summary tables
* Filters

---

## 13. Department-Specific Active Status

The frontend shall display the backend-calculated `department_active_status`.

The frontend shall not independently redefine the business rule.

### HR

```text
employment_status = EMPLOYED
        ↓
ACTIVE
```

### Operations

```text
work_status = WORKING or ONLINE
        ↓
ACTIVE
```

### Finance

```text
salary_status = PAID
        ↓
ACTIVE
```

Otherwise:

```text
NOT ACTIVE
```

The backend remains the authoritative source for this calculated business status.

