## 25. Performance Considerations

The frontend should:

* Avoid unnecessary API calls.
* Load data asynchronously.
* Reuse API results where appropriate.
* Avoid unnecessary component re-renders.
* Use pagination for large datasets.
* Use appropriate chart rendering techniques.
* Keep components modular.

---

## 26. Future Authentication & Authorization

Authentication and authorization are future enhancements.

Potential roles include:

```text
HR Administrator
HR Manager
Operations Manager
Finance Manager
Recruitment User
Management User
Employee
```

Future access control shall be enforced primarily by the backend.

The frontend shall hide or disable functionality based on permissions only as a user-experience measure; backend authorization shall remain authoritative.

---

## 27. Power BI Integration

The HR360 frontend and Power BI analytics layer shall remain logically separated.

The architecture is:

```text
PostgreSQL
     |
     +------> HR360 Backend ------> React Frontend
     |
     +------> Power BI
```

The React application will provide operational dashboards while Power BI will provide advanced business intelligence and reporting.

---

## 28. Git & Source Control

Frontend source code shall be maintained in Git.

Recommended development cycle:

```text
Create Feature
      ↓
Develop
      ↓
Test
      ↓
Git Status
      ↓
Git Add
      ↓
Git Commit
      ↓
Git Push
```

Commits should describe the completed change.

Examples:

```text
Add HR dashboard layout
Add employee management UI
Integrate employee APIs
Add attendance dashboard
Add recruitment pages
Add analytics charts
```

---

## 29. Non-Functional Requirements Alignment

The frontend shall support the following existing requirements:

| Requirement     | Frontend Implementation      |
| --------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Usability       | Consistent navigation and UI |
| Performance     | Efficient API usage          |
| Reliability     | Loading/error handling       |
| Maintainability | Modular components           |
| Scalability     | Feature-based architecture   |
| Security        | Backend-mediated API access  |
| Compatibility   | Modern browser support       |

